    "body": "_Requested by **Sia**_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Order: independent; safe to merge anytime (follows #409 and #411, already in main).\n- Depends on: nothing open.\n- If merged out of order with #415, #418, #419, #420, #421 (DEVONthink stack): they only edit the module table near line 164 of `sp-academic.org`; this PR edits the Citar section near line 3130 and `sp-citations.el`, so no conflict is expected.\n- After merging: nothing to retarget.\n\n## Summary\n\n- **Order:** the columns are now emoji, authors, year, title, citekey, then keywords/tags (`citar-templates`), and `sp-citations-column-priorities` is `1 2 1 2 1 3`, so emoji, year and the 45-column citekey are served first and always fit.\n- **Alignment (likely cause):** every column position is counted from the left of the window, but Vertico draws a two-column cursor mark before the indicators. The first column started two places later than counted, so a value that filled its column (the 45-character citekey, a long title) pushed the next column right of the other rows. New `sp-citations-prefix-width` (2) is added to the block width, so the positions are right.\n- **If it is still off:** adjust `sp-citations-prefix-width` (try 0, 1, 3); the cause is a guess from the code, not seen in the GUI.\n- New tests: `tests/sp-citations-columns-test.el` (column starts equal across rows, order and widths); tangle check passes.\n- Docs updated in `docs/tangles/academic/sp-academic.org` (bullet lists). No CHANGELOG edit.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] Pull this branch, restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`), then `M-x citar-refresh` (untested by Claude: GUI)\n- [ ] `C-c w b o` (`citar-open`) with the posframe on: columns read emoji, author, year, title, citekey, keywords (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] Scroll through many rows: every column starts at the same place in every row, including rows with the longest citekey and the longest title (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] A citekey of 45+ characters shows its first 45 characters; the year is never cut\n- [ ] Edge: narrow the frame; the title and authors shrink first, emoji, year and citekey stay whole\n- [x] If columns are shifted by 1 or 2 places: `M-x customize-variable RET sp-citations-prefix-width`, try 0, 1 or 3 and run `citar-refresh`; tell me the value that lines up\n- [x] Regression: `M-x citar-create-note` and `citar-insert-citation` still show the indicators 🌿️ 📁️ 📝️ 🎓️ and the entry-type emoji\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- Discard local edits: `git -C ~/dotfiles status`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .` (`git clean -fd` only after checking `git clean -nd`).\n- Back to main: `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles pull`.\n- Optionally delete the test branch locally: `git -C ~/dotfiles branch -D claude/citar-column-order-alignment` (the remote copy stays until the PR is merged or closed).\n- Restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`) and run `citar-refresh` so the config matches main again.\n- This PR changes no notes or vault files, so there is nothing to restore there.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9m8fmtgNiBeMPZDGW)_",
